              "text": "mōtus, mōtūs — \"a movement; a stirring (of the mind); a disturbance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Magnus mōtus in urbe fuit. There was a great commotion in the city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōtus, mōtūs m., from moveō. Mōtus animī, a stirring of the mind; mōtus terrae, an earthquake. English motion and motor belong to the family."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mōtus is the noun built on moveō \"to move\" (Lewis & Short), from its participle mōtus. English motion and motor belong to the same family."
            }
          ]
